.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> My schedule looks like this:<br /> <br /> 1-Vehicles<br /> 1-Possibly Psiads, Superiors and Anima<br /> <br /> <br /> I created around 20 characters for testing. You can use them...if you need more, just talk.<br /> <br /> If you want to use the Sheet, just get in touch and I'll create a room with the sheet. It would be nice for the feedbacks.<br /> <br /> The room link is:<br /> <br /> <br /> <u><b><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><a href=\"https://app.roll20.net/join/10870153/X81x-Q\" target=\"_blank\">https://app.roll20.net/join/10870153/X81x-Q</a></span></b></u><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26537,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26537-jonnes-derik","user":"Jonnes.Derik","date":". 12-03-2021, 11:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26537-jonnes-derik","name":"Jonnes.Derik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26537_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-03T10:39:27-08:00","id":1469505,"title":"","content":"If possible it would be cool if you had a option for novas to have above 5 in attributes if storytellers house ruled the superior attribute edge so novas can take it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26058-aeonstorm","name":"Aeonstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-06T07:55:17-08:00","id":1469732,"title":"","content":"Sheet will have implementation for NPCs AND Antagonists Template format also? It was a problem on Scion sheet for Roll20...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-06-2021, 11:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-07T05:14:14-08:00","id":1469822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sheet will have implementation for NPCs AND Antagonists Template format also? It was a problem on Scion sheet for Roll20... </div> </div> </div>Yep ^^. It is already developed in the Roll-20 room on the link, in the &quot;Template&quot; field.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26537-jonnes-derik","name":"Jonnes.Derik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26537_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-01T19:24:56-08:00","id":1471640,"title":"","content":"Working on making a Psion character for practice and have a few notes.<br /> <br /> Under Aptitude Clairsentience is spelled &quot;CLAIRSENTENTE&quot;<br /> <br /> Under Clairsentience the basic power 'The Sight' is spelled &quot;The Sigth&quot;<br /> <br /> When expanding a Mode dot level to see the description it expands all three at that level. Not sure if this was intentional or not, but I noted that other sections with similar layout don't do this (weapon tags for instance) so wanted to flag it. <br /> <br /> Edit button on Auxiliary Modes lets you drag an entire row up or down but little else. Seems like it would be better if you were able to reorder a single card, and delete it in case you added it in error. (same thing happens with weapons, gear, and armor)<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-06T07:37:02-08:00","id":1471936,"title":"","content":"Thank you so much for taking the time to give feedback. <br /> <br /> So the terms &quot;Clairsentience&quot; has already been fixed in the latest version. The term &quot;The Sigth&quot; will be corrected in the next update (already changed it in the source code). <br /> <br /> Regarding the Expand behavior, it's working as expected. <br /> <br /> Regarding Edit button on Auxiliary Modes. I tried so hard to implement the behavior where you would have autonomy to manipulate a single card. But unfortunately, with the limitations of the roll-20, it wasn't possible. I'm hoping they evolve this Repeating Section module, only then will it be possible to leave it with the expected behavior. <br /> <br /> Again, Thank you so much for the Feedback.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26537-jonnes-derik","name":"Jonnes.Derik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26537_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-07T08:39:18-08:00","id":1472001,"title":"","content":"Thank you for working on this! It is amazing and I'm excited to be able to use when I run an Aeon game later this year!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-30T11:33:07-08:00","id":1473588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeonstorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1454279-character-sheet-trinity-continnum-character-sheet-project-for-roll-20?p=1469505#post1469505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If possible it would be cool if you had a option for novas to have above 5 in attributes if storytellers house ruled the superior attribute edge so novas can take it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Novas can already take the superior trait edge. Powered edges may be taken by talents, novas, and psi users. i think every version of the sheet should be expanded to 6 dots and psiads and psions should go to 7 dots. Otherwise this is a first class work for Roll20. I am very impressed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1580-andrewm9","name":"andrewm9","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-31T09:45:54-08:00","id":1473675,"title":"","content":"So, I already had some debates with my brother, about the dot numbers of these Tiers.<br /> <br /> Regarding Novas, as you can see on page 183 of TC:Aberrant it says: &quot;For nova, Mega-Attributes replace the higher-Tier ability to raise regular abilities above a rating of 5; nova that have abilities have greater dots in Mega-Attributes instead.&quot; With that, Novas does not have the sixth dot. They jump to the next Mega-Attribute dot.<br /> <br /> Regarding the seventh dot in Psions. I'm really not convinced there is a seventh Dot. From what I understand from the rules, when getting the Tier Proxy, the character unlocks the Sixth in all attributes, which can be bought normally, without the need for the Powered Edge. That's the understanding I'm following. If any Dev says otherwise, I will implement the change.<br /> <br /> Thank you very, very much for taking the time to give your feedback. My brother and I are working very hard to deliver the best possible... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26537-jonnes-derik","name":"Jonnes.Derik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26537_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-08T15:59:33-08:00","id":1474236,"title":"","content":"Its not so much about the higher Tier, but everyone that is powered can take Superior Trait including novas and talents, so potentially with that edge for 6 xp they can buy one trait up to 6. In theory they can do this 8 more times and raise every trait to 6 assuming they want to burn all that xp. It under Power Edges on page 66 of the Trinity Continuum core rule book.<br /> <br /> Psions (but not Psiads) when they hit tier 3 (proxy tier) can now buy any trait up to 6. When combined along with the Superior Traits Edge they can now buy it up to 7. Many Psion powers also let you temporarily raise traits up to 7 as noted in their power descriptions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1580-andrewm9","name":"andrewm9","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-09T13:07:24-08:00","id":1474317,"title":"","content":"I understand your interpretation, but I don't agree with it at the moment.<br /> <br /> About Proxy Tiers (page 125):<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Proxies are special in that they can gain a sixth Attribute dot in any category without the Extraordinary Attribute Edge, but other Tier 3 characters cannot gain that same benefit. </div> </div> </div>Superior Trait (p 66):<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Your character has some combination of innate ability and special training that allows him to exceed the normal maximum on one Attribute. </div> </div> </div><br /> I believe the normal maximum is 5 dots. So you get the Sixth Dot in two ways. Either you are a Proxy and get the sixth dots slot OR you buy the Superior Trait, to buy the sixth slot for a single attribute.<br /> <br /> They never add up...both give you access only to the Sixth Dot, since in none of the books, a Seventh Dot is mentioned. In fact, there is not even a Seventh dot in the Official Character Sheets.<br /> <br /> So, I will keep that understanding. If by chance, any developer comes to say otherwise, I will make the change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26537-jonnes-derik","name":"Jonnes.Derik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26537_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-09T19:23:21-08:00","id":1474346,"title":"","content":"I think you should get a refund on the exp you spent on extraordinary attribute when you get access to another means of having 6 dots, but I agree that six dots is the max you can get.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27133-planguy","name":"Planguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-10T07:37:02-08:00","id":1474372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think you should get a refund on the exp you spent on extraordinary attribute when you get access to another means of having 6 dots, but I agree that six dots is the max you can get. </div> </div> </div>I agree wint you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26537-jonnes-derik","name":"Jonnes.Derik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26537_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-24T12:01:33-08:00","id":1475415,"title":"","content":"Hey people, Update 5 is ready<br /> <br /> <br /> Roll-20 [Update] Character-Sheet Project for Roll-20<br /> <br /> 1- Expanded<br /> NPC - It is now possible to choose the type of Source Power<br /> <br /> 2- Developed<br /> Psiads<br /> Jinketsu (Supeiors)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div align=\"center\"><img src=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/9hkjy1e6c2b4u1u/NPC.png?raw=1\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/> </div> <div align=\"center\"> NPC - Expanded (Source type Available)<br /> <br /> <br /> </div> <div align=\"center\"> <img src=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/wkl3ke9akuaaev9/Screenshot_1.png?raw=1\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> NPC - Expanded (Source type Available)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/14eb3p4ya5wob83/Jinketsu.png?raw=1\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> Jinketsu<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/n8q7j9xbxvq1n9y/Psiad%20-%20Advanced.png?raw=1\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> Psiad Default and Advanced</div> <br /> My schedule looks like this:<br /> <br /> 1- Noetic-Tech<br /> 2- Possibly Anima, Vargs<br /> <br /> <br /> I created around 20 characters for testing. You can use them...if you need more, just talk.<br /> <br /> If you want to use the Sheet, just get in touch and I'll create a room with the sheet. It would be nice for the feedbacks.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>The room link is:</b></span><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://app.roll20.net/join/10870153/X81x-Q\" target=\"_blank\"><b><span style=\"font-size:24px\">https://app.roll20.net/join/10870153/X81x-Q</span></b></a><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26537-jonnes-derik","name":"Jonnes.Derik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26537_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-24T16:36:21-08:00","id":1475422,"title":"","content":"This is some fantastic progress. I can't wait for this to get released!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27302-roboeel","name":"roboeel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-01T10:25:10-08:00","id":1475645,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><img src=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/6jwx8a4iqc2usya/Trinity%20Continuum%20-%20Roll%2020.png?raw=1\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">After nearly a year of development finally Trinity Continuum Character Sheet was released on Roll-20. </span><br /> <br /> On Roll-20 it is listed as <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><u><b>Trinity Continuum 2e</b></u></span></span><br /> <br /> Available Templates:<br /> <i> -Baseline<br /> -Talent<br /> -Nova<br /> -Jinketsu<br /> -Psiad<br /> -Psion<br /> -Inspired<br /> -NPC<br /> -Flux-Tech<br /> -Quantum-Tech<br /> -Vehicles</i><br /> <br /> Upcoming Templates:<br /> <i>-Noetic-Tech<br /> -Anima</i><br /> <div align=\"center\"><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Thanks to everyone who helped or supported the project. <b><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Enjoy and have Fun!!!</span></b></span></div> <br /> <div align=\"center\"><br /> If you want to join the beta testers room, go to:<br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><a href=\"http://app.roll20.net/join/10870153/X81x-Q\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#cc0099\">https://app.roll20.net/join/10870153/X81x-Q</span></a></span></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Suggestions and feedback contact: <br /> <a href=\"http://mercuryclustertc@gmail.com\" target=\"_blank\"><b><span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><span class=\"__cf_email__\" data-cfemail=\"fd90988f9e888f849e91888e89988f899ebd9a909c9491d39e9290\">[email&#160;protected]</span></span></b></a></span><br /> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26537-jonnes-derik","name":"Jonnes.Derik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26537_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-11T08:54:06-08:00","id":1476210,"title":"","content":"FWIW: in the Paths section, &quot;Access&quot; is misspelled as &quot;Acess&quot;. In that same section, &quot;Connections&quot; is misspelled as &quot;Conections&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":912,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/912-gamer-n-geek","user":"Gamer N. Geek","date":". 03-11-2022, 12:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/912-gamer-n-geek","name":"Gamer N. Geek","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-12T20:03:52-08:00","id":1476309,"title":"","content":"Thanks for putting this together! I am currently building out a one shot to run for some folks and really looking forward to it. I did notice a minor issue, the Psi rating can't be dropped below two dots once you increase it that far. While it isn't a big deal during play, if you change your mind during character creation or making a bunch of NPCs it can come up. Easy work around is to just go into the &quot;attribute &amp; Abilities&quot; tab on the char sheet and change the value there, but thought i should mention it. This is the only power source that would do this. All the others let you drop them all the way to zero by clicking on the relevant dot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1162-nazeriel","name":"nazeriel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1162_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-12T20:53:36-08:00","id":1476310,"title":"","content":"Is there a way for other Novas and Inspired to get to the Attribute level of 6 on the sheet that I am missing? While most cannot normally achieve, they can with the Superior Trait edge which anybody but a baseline can take.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1580-andrewm9","name":"andrewm9","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-13T22:39:05-07:00","id":1476362,"title":"","content":"We just used these sheets tonight in my Aeon game and they were fantastic. We haven't really messed with setting up circumstantials or custom rolls yet, but even just having the functionality of the sheet and the dice roller is fantastic, and having all the templates right there on one sheet is great. Thanks so much for this!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27302-roboeel","name":"roboeel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-15T09:56:45-07:00","id":1476440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> FWIW: in the Paths section, &quot;Access&quot; is misspelled as &quot;Acess&quot;. In that same section, &quot;Connections&quot; is misspelled as &quot;Conections&quot;. </div> </div> </div>Thank you very much for the feedback, English is not my first language, so this kind of inconsistency can be quite common. In the next update it will be fixed. <br /> <br /> again thank you very much","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26537-jonnes-derik","name":"Jonnes.Derik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26537_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-15T10:04:14-07:00","id":1476441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Thanks for putting this together! I am currently building out a one shot to run for some folks and really looking forward to it. I did notice a minor issue, the Psi rating can't be dropped below two dots once you increase it that far. While it isn't a big deal during play, if you change your mind during character creation or making a bunch of NPCs it can come up. Easy work around is to just go into the &quot;attribute &amp; Abilities&quot; tab on the char sheet and change the value there, but thought i should mention it. This is the only power source that would do this. All the others let you drop them all the way to zero by clicking on the relevant dot. </div> </div> </div>About PSI points, have a minimum value of 2. It was following the rule, where psychomorphs (Pions and Psiads) have a minimum PSI of 2 and the humanity standard (baseline) is 1. I agree that it seems incongruous that the other Sources (Quantum and Inspiration) can go to zero. I can fix this in the future.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26537-jonnes-derik","name":"Jonnes.Derik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26537_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-15T10:07:48-07:00","id":1476442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is there a way for other Novas and Inspired to get to the Attribute level of 6 on the sheet that I am missing? While most cannot normally achieve, they can with the Superior Trait edge which anybody but a baseline can take. </div> </div> </div>I already have an answer saved in .txt for nova question...lol.<br /> <br /> Regarding Novas, as you can see on page 183 of TC:Aberrant it says:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;For nova, Mega-Attributes replace the higher-Tier ability to raise regular abilities above a rating of 5; nova that have abilities have greater dots in Mega- Attributes instead.&quot; </div> </div> </div>With that, Novas does not have the sixth dot. They jump to the next Mega-Attribute dot.<br /> <br /> <br /> But you're absolutely right about the sixth dot in the inspired. Will be fixed in the next update<br /> <br /> Thank you so much for taking the time for feedback.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26537,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26537-jonnes-derik","user":"Jonnes.Derik","date":". 03-15-2022, 01:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26537-jonnes-derik","name":"Jonnes.Derik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26537_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-15T10:12:40-07:00","id":1476443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We just used these sheets tonight in my Aeon game and they were fantastic. We haven't really messed with setting up circumstantials or custom rolls yet, but even just having the functionality of the sheet and the dice roller is fantastic, and having all the templates right there on one sheet is great. Thanks so much for this! </div> </div> </div>Thank you very much, roboeel. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26537-jonnes-derik","name":"Jonnes.Derik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26537_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-15T13:57:01-07:00","id":1476458,"title":"","content":"Fixed, take a look at the Roll-20!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26537-jonnes-derik","name":"Jonnes.Derik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26537_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-15T18:13:38-07:00","id":1476481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jonnes.Derik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1454279-character-sheet-trinity-continnum-character-sheet-project-for-roll-20?p=1476442#post1476442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I already have an answer saved in .txt for nova question...lol.<br /> <br /> Regarding Novas, as you can see on page 183 of TC:Aberrant it says:<br /> <br /> With that, Novas does not have the sixth dot. They jump to the next Mega-Attribute dot.<br /> <br /> <br /> But you're absolutely right about the sixth dot in the inspired. Will be fixed in the next update<br /> <br /> Thank you so much for taking the time for feedback.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I am referring to has nothing to do with being higher tier and everything to do with the Superior Trait Edge found on page 66 of the Trinity Continuum rulebook which lets you raise your attribute 1 above whatever your tier is and is open to any powered person from Talents to Novas (I assume Superiors/Jinketsu gain access to it also). Normally Inspired, Talents, Novas or quite frankly anybody who is not a Tier 3 Psion, Psiad, or Superior can't raise it to 6 at all, but that Edge lets them do so for one specific attribute.<br /> <br /> Don't take my continuing question as an argument or nasty criticism, just trying to get it right for my players and I who will truly appreciate your work. Thanks for that. I've included the relevant text from the book below.<br /> <br /> &quot;Your character has some combination of innate<br /> ability and special training that allows him to exceed<br /> the normal maximum on one Attribute. This Edge<br /> does not increase the Attribute; it merely allows<br /> you to be able to spend Experience to raise it to its<br /> new maximum. This Edge may be purchased multiple<br /> times, each time for a different Attribute, i.e. the<br /> same Attribute may not be raised a second time.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1580-andrewm9","name":"andrewm9","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-15T20:31:33-07:00","id":1476494,"title":"","content":"andrewm9, I didn't take it as an argument or nasty criticism at all. I only mentioned the .txt save as a fun fact, but in no way was it making you feel bad. If so, please forgive me.<br /> <br /> So, still using the rule I mentioned above, it gives page 183 of TC - Aberrant:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For nova, Mega-Attributes replace the higher-Tier ability to raise regular abilities above a rating of 5; nova that have abilities have greater dots in Mega-Attributes instead. </div> </div> </div>The understanding followed was: Novas do not have a sixth dot at all. If by chance, the player wants to buy this Edge, specifically Novas jump from the fifth dot, to Mega Attribute 1, as stated in the rule above.<br /> <br /> In fact, I think our point of disagreement is the precedence of rules. Clearly these rules are conflicting. My understanding is: As Trinity Continuum: Aberrant is the most recent book, its rules take precedence over Trinity Continuum:Core (as do the Scale rules), especially for Nova Age.<br /> <br /> But, If by chance a Dev clarifies that Novas do in fact have a sixth dot. I adjust the Sheet.<br /> <br /> Again sorry if you felt attacked in any way by my comment, it really wasn't the intention. And thank you so much for taking the time to improve the sheet.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26537,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26537-jonnes-derik","user":"Jonnes.Derik","date":". 03-15-2022, 11:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26537-jonnes-derik","name":"Jonnes.Derik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26537_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-16T07:38:47-07:00","id":1476520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jonnes.Derik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1454279-character-sheet-trinity-continnum-character-sheet-project-for-roll-20?p=1476494#post1476494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">andrewm9, I didn't take it as an argument or nasty criticism at all. I only mentioned the .txt save as a fun fact, but in no way was it making you feel bad. If so, please forgive me.<br /> <br /> So, still using the rule I mentioned above, it gives page 183 of TC - Aberrant:<br /> <br /> <br /> The understanding followed was: Novas do not have a sixth dot at all. If by chance, the player wants to buy this Edge, specifically Novas jump from the fifth dot, to Mega Attribute 1, as stated in the rule above.<br /> <br /> In fact, I think our point of disagreement is the precedence of rules. Clearly these rules are conflicting. My understanding is: As Trinity Continuum: Aberrant is the most recent book, its rules take precedence over Trinity Continuum:Core (as do the Scale rules), especially for Nova Age.<br /> <br /> But, If by chance a Dev clarifies that Novas do in fact have a sixth dot. I adjust the Sheet.<br /> <br /> Again sorry if you felt attacked in any way by my comment, it really wasn't the intention. And thank you so much for taking the time to improve the sheet.</div> </div> </div> </div>No offense taken, I just wanted to be clear and not give offense either. Thanks for going over your logic. I don\u2019t see the conflict myself, but its not the end of the world and the sheet is great to use, easy too. Thanks for taking the hard work out of it. For my PC\u2019s that have, I can just have them add an extra die to the roll in question when and if it comes up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1580-andrewm9","name":"andrewm9","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-05T20:06:03-07:00","id":1478113,"title":"","content":"Would <b>TC Roll20</b> char sheet handle <b>TC Adventure</b> simple characters? I plan to run the game in next 3 months, I think about options for VTT.<br /> <br /> In general, you can also answer how support will look for next <b>TC</b> era settings:<ul><li><b>Assassins</b></li> <li><b>Anima</b></li> <li><b>Aeon</b></li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-05-2022, 11:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-05T21:02:05-07:00","id":1478116,"title":"","content":"Honestly, Adventure, Assassins and Anima (real world) all use only Talents sheets, so I dont see any reason to change the sheet.<br /> <br /> Anima Anima sheets would need a different sheet, for sure, but its in the list and we dont have the final rules of Anima yet to be honest.<br /> <br /> If there is one rule system not covered that is ready is the system from NWE. But its not a big deal.<br /> <br /> Great job in the sheets by the way!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-06T00:53:34-07:00","id":1478122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1454279-character-sheet-trinity-continnum-character-sheet-project-for-roll-20?p=1478116#post1478116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, Adventure, Assassins and Anima (real world) all use only Talents sheets, so I dont see any reason to change the sheet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does not <b>Adventure!</b> use other Trinity splats as <b>Mesmerists</b> ( Psions ) and <b>Stalwarts</b> ( Novas )? Are those recreated in Roll20 sheet?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/trinity-continuum-adventure-tabletop-roleplaying-game/description\" target=\"_blank\">Main KS descripton</a>:<br /> <i>'After the explosion of Doctor Sir Calvin Hammersmith\u2019s \u201ctelluric engine\u201d early in the 20th century, people the world over begin to demonstrate extraordinary capabilities. <b>Stalwart</b> individuals with the strength to pull a safe from a wall, or the quickness of hand to pluck a bullet from the air. <b>Mesmerists</b> with the ability to cloud mens\u2019 minds or see visions of distant places. Valiant daredevils with unparalleled skill or luck. Collectively called the Inspired, the newly-formed \u00c6on Society for Gentlemen is on a mission to guide the Inspired, catalog telluric phenomena, and shepherd humanity to a better place.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-06-2022, 04:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-06T00:58:40-07:00","id":1478123,"title":"","content":"Mesmerists and Stalwarts, while not Talents, work as Talents by the rules, much like Assassins. They have their own Gifts and special Dramatic Editing rules, and their gifts use a different thematic, but yet, they fit the same char sheet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-06T10:32:12-07:00","id":1478156,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>About Adventure! Characters</b></span><br /> The sheet already supports Adventure characters! There listed as Inspired. The template is very similar to Talents, as Mateus Luz mentioned, it only changes Sheet's &quot;Skin&quot;.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>About Assassins</b></span><br /> I have no plans to add Assassins at the moment. But if I develop something like that, I would do it as a subdivision of Talents. But I think it's perfectly possible to play Assassins using the Talent Sheet at the moment.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">About Anima </span></b><br /> I'm working on it right now, very soon I'll make it available in the testing room.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>About Aeon </b></span><br /> Almost all templates (as far as I remember) are now available. Like Psion, Proxys, Psiad default, Psiad Advanced and Jinketsu. Noetic and Varg Technologies will be developed... one day.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Probably after Anima, I'll work on Cybernetics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26537-jonnes-derik","name":"Jonnes.Derik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26537_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-06T10:34:53-07:00","id":1478157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1454279-character-sheet-trinity-continnum-character-sheet-project-for-roll-20?p=1478116#post1478116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, Adventure, Assassins and Anima (real world) all use only Talents sheets, so I dont see any reason to change the sheet.<br /> <br /> Anima Anima sheets would need a different sheet, for sure, but its in the list and we dont have the final rules of Anima yet to be honest.<br /> <br /> If there is one rule system not covered that is ready is the system from NWE. But its not a big deal.<br /> <br /> Great job in the sheets by the way!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks, Mateus Luz ^^<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26537-jonnes-derik","name":"Jonnes.Derik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26537_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-08T19:00:42-07:00","id":1478314,"title":"","content":"I've been setting up some NPCs using the sheet and have a suggestion, Chromatics and Qin can have Modes from a few different Aptitude so the options for psi don't quite work for them. It would be awesome if the NPC Source dropdown had an option for like 'Psi-Alien' that would work like 'Psi-Psiad' but lack the Quantakinesis section, and have the cap on modes removed (psionic aliens usually have different caps on modes, no need to try and make the sheet account for all of them).<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4270,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","user":"literatzi","date":".  tweaked the wording around caps on modes 04-09-2022, 10:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-10T18:55:45-07:00","id":1478537,"title":"","content":"How do you get to the character sheets?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-11T10:02:41-07:00","id":1478578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>literatzi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1454279-character-sheet-trinity-continnum-character-sheet-project-for-roll-20?p=1478314#post1478314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been setting up some NPCs using the sheet and have a suggestion, Chromatics and Qin can have Modes from a few different Aptitude so the options for psi don't quite work for them. It would be awesome if the NPC Source dropdown had an option for like 'Psi-Alien' that would work like 'Psi-Psiad' but lack the Quantakinesis section, and have the cap on modes removed (psionic aliens usually have different caps on modes, no need to try and make the sheet account for all of them).<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Very interesting idea. I promise I will carefully consider this. Thank you for sharing<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26537-jonnes-derik","name":"Jonnes.Derik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26537_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-11T10:12:16-07:00","id":1478579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1454279-character-sheet-trinity-continnum-character-sheet-project-for-roll-20?p=1478537#post1478537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you get to the character sheets?</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't quite understand your question. I'll assume you want access to the sheets. For this you make an account in the roll-20. Create a room and select the Trinity Continuum 2ed sheet. <br /> <br /> You can enter the test room, there you will have the latest updates, before going to the submitted version. The sheet of Anima, based on the manuscripts, will soon be placed in the testing room.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><u><b>Test Room</b></u>:</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b><a href=\"https://app.roll20.net/join/10870153/X81x-Q\" target=\"_blank\">https://app.roll20.net/join/10870153/X81x-Q</a></b></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26537-jonnes-derik","name":"Jonnes.Derik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26537_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-16T18:36:25-07:00","id":1478994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jonnes.Derik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1454279-character-sheet-trinity-continnum-character-sheet-project-for-roll-20?p=1478579#post1478579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I didn't quite understand your question. I'll assume you want access to the sheets. For this you make an account in the roll-20. Create a room and select the Trinity Continuum 2ed sheet.<br /> <br /> You can enter the test room, there you will have the latest updates, before going to the submitted version. The sheet of Anima, based on the manuscripts, will soon be placed in the testing room.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><u><b>Test Room</b></u>:</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b><a href=\"https://app.roll20.net/join/10870153/X81x-Q\" target=\"_blank\">https://app.roll20.net/join/10870153/X81x-Q</a></b></span></div> </div> </div> </div>When I go to the test area and launch the game, I do eventually get to various characters, but what I really want are the blank template sheets especially for Superior and Psiads.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-19T08:14:05-07:00","id":1479131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Origina