.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1454279-character-sheet-trinity-continnum-character-sheet-project-for-roll-20?p=1494339#post1494339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For these cases, I recommend Custom Rolls in the Rolls Tab, where you can save your custom rolls.</div> </div> </div> </div>How can I save Custom Rolls? \ud83e\udd14 I could make custom one roll - but could not save the design on later... \ud83d\ude14","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-06T06:35:14-07:00","id":1494455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1454279-character-sheet-trinity-continnum-character-sheet-project-for-roll-20?p=1494382#post1494382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How can I save Custom Rolls? \ud83e\udd14 I could make custom one roll - but could not save the design on later... \ud83d\ude14</div> </div> </div> </div>Go to the 'Rolls' tab in the character sheet, 'Custom Rolls' is the top section. If you hit the expand arrow you can define the dice pools rolled, and you name the roll at the top. During play you can just go to Rolls and hit the dice icon for a custom roll and it will roll like normal.<br /> <br /> The 'Rolls' tab is really good for setting up common rolls that have specific enhancement or are affected by Edges, so you don't have to type them in constantly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-06T17:16:30-07:00","id":1494480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>literatzi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1454279-character-sheet-trinity-continnum-character-sheet-project-for-roll-20?p=1494455#post1494455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Go to the 'Rolls' tab in the character sheet, 'Custom Rolls' is the top section. If you hit the expand arrow you can define the dice pools rolled, and you name the roll at the top. During play you can just go to Rolls and hit the dice icon for a custom roll and it will roll like normal.<br /> <br /> The 'Rolls' tab is really good for setting up common rolls that have specific enhancement or are affected by Edges, so you don't have to type them in constantly.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Precisely!!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26537-jonnes-derik","name":"Jonnes.Derik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26537_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-03T01:13:49-08:00","id":1498655,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26537-jonnes-derik\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26537_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26537\" data-vbnamecard=\"26537\">Jonnes.Derik</a> Trinity Core rules points that PCs Talents ALSO have Defense Rating that is generally 1 - but can be higher. I do not see this rating on PCs variants of sheets...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trinity Core rulebook, p. 38</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>DEFENSE</b><br /> A character\u2019s standard Defense is 1. Characters can attempt to make a defensive action when being <br /> attacked by rolling whichever Resilience Attribute makes the most sense, with no Skill added (see p. <br /> 105).</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-03T19:04:15-08:00","id":1498721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1454279-character-sheet-trinity-continnum-character-sheet-project-for-roll-20?p=1498655#post1498655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26537-jonnes-derik\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26537_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26537\" data-vbnamecard=\"26537\">Jonnes.Derik</a> Trinity Core rules points that PCs Talents ALSO have Defense Rating that is generally 1 - but can be higher. I do not see this rating on PCs variants of sheets...<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There isn't a specific spot for it on the sheet, but since it will almost always be 1 you don't really need an area to track that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-04T07:26:30-08:00","id":1498759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>literatzi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1454279-character-sheet-trinity-continnum-character-sheet-project-for-roll-20?p=1498721#post1498721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There isn't a specific spot for it on the sheet, but since it will almost always be 1 you don't really need an area to track that.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, <i><b>Defense</b> <u>can be </u>higher than 1 </i>for character with proper Equipment or Powers active. Not to mention Tokens on Roll20 SHOULD have Defense pointed from tokens colored circles. ( I can point them myself - but main sheet need Defense trait to use it then. ) On NPC sheets I can point Defense of enemies easily.<br /> <br /> Also, official sheet points to this number-<br /> <b><i>'Defense = Appropriate Resilience Attribute' </i></b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>'Trinity Core Rulebook p. 153</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Talented Defense</b> \u2014 The player may spend a point of Inspiration to gain a bonus to the character\u2019s Defense equal to her lowest-rated Facet for the rest of the scene.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>'Trinity Core Rulebook p. 205</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>MOVING TARGET</b><br /> Keywords: Constant, Skill (Athletics)<br /> Prerequisite: Athletics \u2022\u2022<br /> (...)<br /> <b>System: </b>The character always has one additional point of Defense. If she fails her Defensive action roll, the Difficulty to hit her is 2 instead of 1.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>'Trinity Core Rulebook p. 138</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Defense: </b> This is the base Defense for the antagonist. Dodge and soft armor are both folded into this Trait. If something would affect an opponent\u2019s armor rating or Defense, apply it directly to this Defense rating.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-04-2022, 10:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-04T10:02:10-08:00","id":1498774,"title":"","content":"Other issue raised by my players - <b>When using Core Roll</b>, you cannot edit name of it, to show what you doing on Roll20 chat. We wanted to put things like <i>'Hitting X'</i> or <i>'Persuade'</i> instead of <i>'Core Roll'</i>.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://imgur.com/98rZ2zM\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/98rZ2zM.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-04-2022, 01:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-07T04:25:23-08:00","id":1499050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1454279-character-sheet-trinity-continnum-character-sheet-project-for-roll-20?p=1498655#post1498655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26537-jonnes-derik\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26537_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26537\" data-vbnamecard=\"26537\">Jonnes.Derik</a> Trinity Core rules points that PCs Talents ALSO have Defense Rating that is generally 1 - but can be higher. I do not see this rating on PCs variants of sheets...<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The Circunstantials tab is just for these cases, for character default stat modifiers.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26537-jonnes-derik","name":"Jonnes.Derik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26537_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-07T04:33:13-08:00","id":1499051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1454279-character-sheet-trinity-continnum-character-sheet-project-for-roll-20?p=1498774#post1498774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Other issue raised by my players - <b>When using Core Roll</b>, you cannot edit name of it, to show what you doing on Roll20 chat. We wanted to put things like <i>'Hitting X'</i> or <i>'Persuade'</i> instead of <i>'Core Roll'</i>.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://imgur.com/98rZ2zM\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/98rZ2zM.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> </div> </div> </div>Cores rolls were designed for trivial rolls, (attributes and skills) with the standard difficulty of the tier. <br /> <br /> For more specific rolls, Customs Rolls have been developed, which can be saved. There you can define all the stats and define a name, for these more specific rolls..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26537-jonnes-derik","name":"Jonnes.Derik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26537_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-07T10:38:18-08:00","id":1499077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jonnes.Derik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1454279-character-sheet-trinity-continnum-character-sheet-project-for-roll-20?p=1499050#post1499050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Circunstantials tab is just for these cases, for character default stat modifiers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not get how <b>Circunstantials</b> generate <b>Defense</b> trait for use with T<b>oken Bars</b>. Is this show in sheet instruction video? If yes - on what time it is?<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/XeMfg9S.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-07T14:34:17-08:00","id":1499101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1454279-character-sheet-trinity-continnum-character-sheet-project-for-roll-20?p=1499077#post1499077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not get how <b>Circunstantials</b> generate <b>Defense</b> trait for use with T<b>oken Bars</b>. Is this show in sheet instruction video? If yes - on what time it is?<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/XeMfg9S.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately, Circumstantial Tab stats do not appear on Token Bars. You have two &quot;<b>official</b>&quot; options and two &quot;<b>Hack mode</b>&quot; options. <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Official ones:</span></b><ul><li>manually add defense on Token Bars.</li> </ul><ul><li>use the Circumstantial Tab itself for reference.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Hack mode&quot;</span></b><ul><li>In Roll-20 you can add your own attributes in the &quot;Attributes &amp; Abilities&quot; tab (at the top of the sheet, next to Character Sheet and Bio &amp; Info). Click + Add and name the attribute as you like. The newly created Attribute becomes an option for the Tokens Bar.</li> </ul><ul><li>The other option is to Switch to the NPC template, increment the defense trait, and then switch to the desired template. In tokens bar look for npc_defence, and use the value as a reference. If you want to change the value, just switch to the NPC template, make the change and return to the desired template.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> It's not pretty, but it works.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26537-jonnes-derik","name":"Jonnes.Derik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26537_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-07T20:53:55-08:00","id":1499113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jonnes.Derik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1454279-character-sheet-trinity-continnum-character-sheet-project-for-roll-20?p=1499101#post1499101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not pretty, but it works.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I know about those hacks and I use them to this day. However, should not this trait be core feature of sheet?<br /> <br /> <b>Should you not simply add <i>Defense</i> line in next greater sheet update?</b> Adding <b><i>Defense</i></b> line should not be very hard thing to do for version 10 of TC sheet.<br /> <br /> I understand that adding option for naming Core rolls can be a lot of work - as it needs in depth hack into roll macros - but adding constant one trait as Defense in sheet really should not be.<br /> <br /> / I've made my own house fork from <b>CoD</b> 2E sheet and consulted on <b>Realms of Pugmire</b> ones for Roll20. \ud83d\ude0e /","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-07-2022, 11:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-08T07:43:21-08:00","id":1499143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1454279-character-sheet-trinity-continnum-character-sheet-project-for-roll-20?p=1499113#post1499113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I know about those hacks and I use them to this day. However, should not this trait be core feature of sheet?<br /> <br /> <b>Should you not simply add <i>Defense</i> line in next greater sheet update?</b> Adding <b><i>Defense</i></b> line should not be very hard thing to do for version 10 of TC sheet.<br /> <br /> I understand that adding option for naming Core rolls can be a lot of work - as it needs in depth hack into roll macros - but adding constant one trait as Defense in sheet really should not be.<br /> <br /> / I've made my own house fork from <b>CoD</b> 2E sheet and consulted on <b>Realms of Pugmire</b> ones for Roll20. \ud83d\ude0e /</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You should make your own branch of this sheet and make the changes you want to see if this is a huge deal and easy to add. Joness has already done a ton of work for the community and commented previously they're probably going to move on to new projects with their free time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-08T17:47:03-08:00","id":1499177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>literatzi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1454279-character-sheet-trinity-continnum-character-sheet-project-for-roll-20?p=1499143#post1499143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You should make your own branch of this sheet and make the changes you want to see if this is a huge deal and easy to add. Joness has already done a ton of work for the community and commented previously they're probably going to move on to new projects with their free time.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks so much for the recognition, Literatzi. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26537-jonnes-derik","name":"Jonnes.Derik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26537_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-08T18:12:50-08:00","id":1499180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1454279-character-sheet-trinity-continnum-character-sheet-project-for-roll-20?p=1499113#post1499113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I know about those hacks and I use them to this day. However, should not this trait be core feature of sheet?<br /> <br /> <b>Should you not simply add <i>Defense</i> line in next greater sheet update?</b> Adding <b><i>Defense</i></b> line should not be very hard thing to do for version 10 of TC sheet.<br /> <br /> I understand that adding option for naming Core rolls can be a lot of work - as it needs in depth hack into roll macros - but adding constant one trait as Defense in sheet really should not be.<br /> <br /> / I've made my own house fork from <b>CoD</b> 2E sheet and consulted on <b>Realms of Pugmire</b> ones for Roll20. \ud83d\ude0e /</div> </div> </div> </div>Simply adding a trait is really not a complicated job. But whenever I develop a sheet, I think of the best information architecture I can think of. Where and why to place each unit of information. The entire sheet needs to be cohesive, both in Usability and in the Aesthetics of the elements. And maybe, it's these usability choices, which consume more work and time... So for me, putting a trait is not that easy. <br /> <br /> As for Defense, there is already a suitable place to store it. which are the Circumstantials. It's really a pity that she doesn't appear in the Token Bars. But as I said before, you have options to not be completely unassisted. <br /> <br /> There are some things I still want to do on this Sheet that my work and time don't allow, like Noetic-tech and Cybernetics. But Defense is still not a priority yet. Maybe a future Combat-Mode...but I can't promise anything (I've been working on this project for over a year). <br /> <br /> As for the Core ROlls, it's actually a design decision to keep them the way they are. They were designed for trivial rolls and that's all. What you want, are in the Customs Rolls there, you can customize all the traits of the rolls and leave them saved. <br /> <br /> Sorry if these aren't the answers you wanted. But thank you so much for caring about this project, I try to read all feedback and give some response.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26537-jonnes-derik","name":"Jonnes.Derik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26537_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-13T13:20:20-08:00","id":1499569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jonnes.Derik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1454279-character-sheet-trinity-continnum-character-sheet-project-for-roll-20?p=1499177#post1499177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Thanks so much for the recognition, Literatzi. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for all the work on this! It's so great to have such a good and complete sheet. I was showing it to one of the players who will be in my TC game and he really loved the circumstantial section, and commented how in our Scion game he had to use a google doc to keep track of the all the little bonuses and things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-15T06:52:56-08:00","id":1499746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jonnes.Derik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1454279-character-sheet-trinity-continnum-character-sheet-project-for-roll-20?p=1478156#post1478156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">About Anima </span></b><br /> I'm working on it right now, very soon I'll make it available in the testing room.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you planning to wait until the final book release to set the anima sheets free into the wild? I'm looking to run an Anima game after the start of the year and would really love to make use of the excellent design you've got up in the testing room.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24779-shisumo","name":"Shisumo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-16T03:58:06-08:00","id":1499850,"title":"","content":"This is the idea. Roll-20 has policies for unreleased games. But I can create a room for you to play with the Anima sheet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26537-jonnes-derik","name":"Jonnes.Derik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26537_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-16T21:08:13-08:00","id":1499929,"title":"","content":"How does that work exactly?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24779-shisumo","name":"Shisumo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-16T21:15:36-08:00","id":1499930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jonnes.Derik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1454279-character-sheet-trinity-continnum-character-sheet-project-for-roll-20?p=1499850#post1499850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is the idea. Roll-20 has policies for unreleased games. But I can create a room for you to play with the Anima sheet.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd be interested also on using Anima sheet beta, if I can. \ud83d\ude0e <br /> <br /> With Anima core in Art Direction and Adventure still not released - I suspect we need to brace ourselves for at least half year before Anima official release. We will see how long it takes my Assassins mini chronicle - but I may even run Aeon story before moving to Anima, at this release pace.. \ud83d\ude14 <br /> <br /> ( At least for Aeon we have great sheets by Jones, already. \ud83d\ude32)<br /> <br /> BTW If Roll20 is limiting sheets for unreleased games - how do we have Adventure sheet already on official release, before the setting/game? \ud83e\udd14","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-18T08:51:51-08:00","id":1500040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ( At least for Aeon we have great sheets by Jones, already. \ud83d\ude32) </div> </div> </div>Thanks<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> BTW If Roll20 is limiting sheets for unreleased games - how do we have Adventure sheet already on official release, before the setting/game? \ud83e\udd14 </div> </div> </div>OMG, you are right. From what I've read, Roll-20 has a ban on unreleased game sheets. I somehow believed that inspired was in the scope of Core, but it really wasn't. Most likely they didn't notice either. <br /> <br /> Now I'm in a dilemma... I don't want to run the risk of having the sheet removed from the collection.... On the other hand, I believe that Adventure! come out this week.....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26537-jonnes-derik","name":"Jonnes.Derik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26537_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-18T09:47:24-08:00","id":1500051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jonnes.Derik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1454279-character-sheet-trinity-continnum-character-sheet-project-for-roll-20?p=1500040#post1500040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand, I believe that Adventure! come out this week.....</div> </div> </div> </div>No, <b>Adventure!</b> did not came out this week - and we do not know when it will be. Even backers did not get it. As Winter Holidays are around corner - I suspect even backer version will not come out till January, even half of month.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-18T10:20:03-08:00","id":1500055,"title":"","content":"I read something in the Monday Notes that hinted at it coming out this week. But if not, I'm afraid I'll have to take the Inspired template off the list and wait until the book has been released.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26537-jonnes-derik","name":"Jonnes.Derik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26537_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-18T18:26:58-08:00","id":1500078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jonnes.Derik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1454279-character-sheet-trinity-continnum-character-sheet-project-for-roll-20?p=1500055#post1500055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I read something in the Monday Notes that hinted at it coming out this week. But if not, I'm afraid I'll have to take the Inspired template off the list and wait until the book has been released.</div> </div> </div> </div>The MMN says &quot;symbols this week... then it'll be ready.&quot;<br /> <br /> That's not the same thing as &quot;ready this week.&quot;<br /> <br /> Mike is and has been working on finishing up the various symbols this week. And when he's done with those (he's not yet) then it'll be ready for the next step in the process.<br /> <br /> Will backers be getting the backer PDF soon? Probably. Was it going to be this week? Unlikely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-19T01:27:30-08:00","id":1500087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1454279-character-sheet-trinity-continnum-character-sheet-project-for-roll-20?p=1500078#post1500078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will backers be getting the backer PDF soon? Probably. Was it going to be this week? Unlikely.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__